    pr_ref:  # f80b
    description: "Discovered during WI-kunag validation (bakeoff on koel, 2026-05-11). The blade analyzer (blade-v1) is correctly registered with languages=[\"blade\"] and the producer emits 4 expected extends_template edges when called directly on koel (4 .blade.php files with @extends). However, blade-v1 NEVER enrolls in the pipeline because the profile detector classifies .blade.php files as language='php' only (does not add 'blade' to detected languages). Evidence: koel run shows 'frameworks: [laravel, vue]' but 'languages' includes 'php' (1054 files) and no 'blade' entry. As a result, all 9 .blade.php files in koel get analyzed by php-v1 only, and no extends_template edges appear in hg.json (count = 0). taxonomy.py:402 has the blade LanguageSpec with extensions=['*.blade.php'], so the wiring exists; the issue is profile.py's per-file extension matching — likely *.php matches before *.blade.php, or the detector picks the first match. Direct-call validation confirms blade producer is correct: analyze_blade(koel) emits 4 extends_template edges matching the @extends directives. Fix direction: make extension matching longest-suffix or specifically check for compound extensions like .blade.php before .php."  # f80b
    fields: {}  # f80b
